From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:47:44 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 320/333] [ae-patch] Add Voice mode: one switch for hands-free
 listening, sending and spoken replies

Tapping the speaker button in the composer now turns on Voice mode. While it is on and idle the mic listens through the server's dictation, a finished sentence plus a 0.6 s grace sends the draft the way the Send button does, the mic is stopped from the send until the reply has been spoken, and it resumes 0.3 s after the last sentence. A pending question card is read aloud with its numbered options and answered by a spoken number, label or label words; anything else goes in as the card's own answer after the grace, and silence never answers a card.

A small caret beside the speaker opens the existing menu, which gains a Voice mode switch on top. Turning Speak replies off turns Voice mode off. The switch tells the server through POST /v1/ae/sessions/{id}/voice so a policy can ask for a spoken-style reply.

The logic lives in two new files (aeVoiceMode.ts and useAeVoiceMode.ts). ComposerMicButton gains a controller handle and a listening callback, the speaker hook returns a speak function, and ChatPage adds about twenty lines in the composer. The new setting has a hint of 140 characters or fewer that names the default.
